Phase 20: Upload Project to GitHub

Now that your Student Portal is working, let's save it on GitHub.

Benefits:

Plain Text
✅ Backup your code
✅ Share with recruiters
✅ Show in interviews
✅ Track changes
✅ Learn Git
 
Step 1: Check Git

Run:

Shell
git --version
 

Example:

Plain Text
git version 2.34.1

If not installed:

Shell
sudo apt update
sudo apt install git -y
Step 2: Go to Project Folder
Shell
cd ~/student_portal

Verify:

Shell
pwd

Output:

Plain Text
/root/student_portal
Step 3: Initialize Git Repository
Shell
git init

Output:

Plain Text
Initialized empty Git repository
Step 4: Check Files
Shell
git status

You will see many files marked:

Plain Text
Untracked files
Step 5: Create .gitignore

Create:

Shell
nano .gitignore

Paste:

Plain Text
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
logs/
students.db

Save:

Plain Text
Ctrl + O
Enter
Ctrl + X
Why Exclude These?
Plain Text
venv/ -> Large virtual environment
__pycache__ -> Python cache
logs/ -> Generated logs




=============

Step 6: Check Status Again
Shell
git status

Notice some files disappear from tracking.

Step 7: Add Files
Shell
git add .

Verify:

Shell
git status

You should see:

Plain Text
Changes to be committed:
Step 8: First Commit
Shell
git commit -m "Initial Student Portal Project"

Example:

Plain Text
[main abc123]
Initial Student Portal Project
Step 9: Create GitHub Repository

Open browser:

Plain Text
https://github.com

Login.

Click:

Plain Text
New Repository

Name:

Plain Text
student-portal

Repository type:

Plain Text
Public

Click:

Plain Text
Create Repository
Step 10: Configure Git User (If Asked)

If Git shows:

Plain Text
Please tell me who you are

Run:

Shell
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
Shell
git config --global user.email "your@email.com"
 

Example:

Shell
git config --global user.name "Hyarel Sonawane"
Step 11: Connect Local Project to GitHub

GitHub will show a URL similar to:

Plain Text
https://github.com/your-username/student-portal.git

Run:

Shell
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/student-portal.git
 

Check:

Shell
git remote -v
 
Step 12: Push Code

Rename branch:

Shell
git branch -M main

Push:

Shell
git push -u origin main

You may be asked to authenticate.

Step 13: Verify Upload

Refresh GitHub Repository.

You should see:

Plain Text
student-portal
 
app.py
 
templates/
add_student.html
students.html
search.html
 
requirements.txt
README.md
Step 14: Create requirements.txt

Generate package list:

Shell
pip freeze > requirements.txt

View:

Shell
cat requirements.txt

Example:

Plain Text
Flask==3.x.x

Commit:

Shell
git add requirements.txt
 
git commit -m "Added requirements"
 
git push
Step 15: Create README.md

Create:

Shell
nano README.md

Paste:

Markdown
# Student Portal
 
A Flask-based Student Management System.
 
## Features
 
- Add Student
- View Students
- Search Students
- Login System
- CSV Export
- SQLite Database
- Logging
 
## Technologies
 
- Python
- Flask
- SQLite
- HTML
- Bootstrap
 
## Run
 
python3 app.py

Commit:

Shell
git add README.md
 
git commit -m "Added README"
 
git push


students.db -> Local database


Final Git Commands Cheat Sheet
Shell
git status
 
git add .
 
git commit -m "message"
 
git push
 
git pull
